Each punch card was it&#x27;s own line of text.<p>By putting the final curly brace on it&#x27;s own card, and hence line, it meant you could add lines to blocks without having to change the old last line.<p>E.g. the following code meant you only had to type a new card and insert it.<p><pre><code>     for(i=0;i&lt;10;i++){         &#x2F;* Card 1 *&#x2F;
          printf(&quot;%d &quot;, i);     &#x2F;* Card 2 *&#x2F;
     }                          &#x2F;* Card 3 *&#x2F;

     for(i=0;i&lt;10;i++){         &#x2F;* Card 1 *&#x2F;
          printf(&quot;%d &quot;, i);     &#x2F;* Card 2 *&#x2F;
          printf(&quot;%d\n&quot;, i*i);  &#x2F;* Card 3 *&#x2F;
     }                          &#x2F;* Card 4 *&#x2F;
</code></pre>
But for following had to edit and replace an old card as well.<p><pre><code>     for(i=0;i&lt;10;i++){         &#x2F;* Card 1 *&#x2F;
          printf(&quot;%d &quot;, i);}    &#x2F;* Card 2 *&#x2F;

     for(i=0;i&lt;10;i++){         &#x2F;* Card 1 *&#x2F;
          printf(&quot;%d &quot;, i);     &#x2F;* Card 2&#x27; *&#x2F;
          printf(&quot;%d\n&quot;, i*i);} &#x2F;* Card 3 *&#x2F;
</code></pre>
This saved a bit of typing and made errors less likely.
